.TH hello-clojure "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Hello Command"
.SH NAME
hello-clojure \- Print a greeting message using a Clojure script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hello-clojure
.RI [ EXIT_CODE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B hello-clojure
is a minimal example command that runs a Clojure script installed in the
.I lib/clojure/
directory of the SMI toolset installation.
It demonstrates that Clojure scripting is correctly set up: the
.B clojure
command of the Clojure CLI is on the PATH, Maven and Clojars dependencies resolve, and the SMI
library location is resolvable.
.PP
The command prints a greeting naming the current working directory and a random UUID made by the
.B clj-uuid
library, and then exits with the requested code.
The exit code is echoed on a second line only when it is non-zero;
a successful run prints the greeting alone.
Passing an explicit
.I EXIT_CODE
makes it possible to verify that exit statuses propagate correctly from the
Clojure script, through the shell wrapper, to the calling shell.
.PP
The script is located by sourcing
.I clojure.sh
via
.BR smi-include (1),
which sets
.BR SMI_CLOJURE_LIB_DIR .
The wrapper then does two things, with the same dependencies given to both as
.B \-Sdeps
data:
.IP 1.
.B clojure \-P
downloads the dependencies into
.I ~/.m2/repository
and caches the classpath, without running anything. Its messages, such as
.BR Downloading: ,
go to standard error, so standard output carries the greeting only.
Once the dependencies are there, this step only checks the cache.
.IP 2.
.B clojure \-M
runs the script with the arguments of the command.
.PP
A failed download stops the command before the script runs.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I EXIT_CODE
Optional integer to exit with, in the range
.B 0
to
.BR 255 ,
the range a POSIX shell can report as the status of a command.
Defaults to
.B 0
when omitted.
An argument that is not an integer, or that falls outside that range, is
rejected and the command exits
.BR 1 ,
rather than raising an error.
Rejected values include
.BR abc ,
.BR 42abc ,
.BR 3.9 ,
.BR \-1 ,
and
.BR 256 .
Any further arguments are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no
.I EXIT_CODE
argument was given.
.TP
.B 1
The
.I EXIT_CODE
argument was not an integer in the range
.B 0
to
.BR 255 .
.TP
.I EXIT_CODE
The value passed on the command line, when valid.
.TP
.B other
The status of
.BR "clojure \-P" ,
when the dependencies could not be downloaded.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $(smi-lib-location)/clojure/hello-clojure.clj
The Clojure script executed by this command.
.TP
.I ~/.m2/repository
Where the dependencies are downloaded.
.SH NOTES
The current directory is the project directory of the Clojure CLI, so a
.I deps.edn
there is merged with the dependencies of the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
hello-clojure
hello-clojure 7; echo $?
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clojure (1),
.BR hello-elixir (1),
.BR hello-groovy (1),
.BR hello-lisp (1),
.BR hello-python (1),
.BR smi-include (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
